Package: quercus
Type: Package
Title: Maximum Likelihood Analysis of Quantitative Genetic Data
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 1994-07-11
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ruth G.", "Shaw", role = "aut",
           comment = "Original Quercus programs"),
    person("Frank H.", "Shaw", role = "aut",
           comment = "Original Quercus programs"))
Description: R interface to the Quercus programs for maximum likelihood (ML)
    and restricted maximum likelihood (REML) estimation of genetic and
    environmental variances and covariances from two-generation pedigree data.
    Four programs are provided: nf3 estimates three variance components
    (additive, dominance/common-environment, environmental) for nested or
    parent-offspring designs; nf6 estimates up to six components from diallel
    data; pcrf1 compares genetic variance-covariance matrices between two
    populations; fend determines minimum array dimensions for a dataset.
    The underlying method is described in Shaw (1987)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1558-5646.1987.tb05870.x> and Shaw and Geyer (1993).
    The original Pascal programs were written by Ruth G. Shaw and Frank H. Shaw
    at the University of Minnesota and supported by NIH (GM09664-02) and NSF
    (BSR-8817756, BSR-8905808, DIR-9112842).
